  "gaps": [
    "The student's chosen concentration is not known; the 9-hour concentration block is recorded as one requirement. Options per capture: General Concentration (9 semester hours from ACCT, ANLY, BUSN, DEFM, ECON, ENTR, FINC, HOSP, HRMT, MGMT, MKTG, RLMT, RTMG, SCMG, TLMT courses not otherwise used); Government Contracting and Acquisitions (DEFM305, DEFM410, DEFM424); Reverse Logistics Management (RLMT301, RLMT304, RLMT305); Transportation and Logistics Management (TLMT311, TLMT331, TLMT341).",
    "RLMT301 (Reverse Logistics concentration) and TLMT311 (Transportation and Logistics concentration) also appear in Major Required; the capture does not state how the 9 concentration hours are satisfied when a concentration course duplicates a major course.",
    "Footnote 2 is attached to both TLMT498 and BUSN499 and states 'Must be taken as the last course before graduation'; the capture does not resolve which course is the final course.",
    "Footnote 1 on Arts & Humanities states literature courses require ENGL101 or ENGL110; specific course choices within the Arts & Humanities, Communication, History, and Natural Sciences selection blocks are not determined.",
    "The capture does not state any residency requirement (credits that must be completed at the institution), so no requirement is marked institutional-only.",
    "The capture does not state course level restrictions (e.g., upper-division minimums) for the General Concentration or elective courses beyond 'undergraduate courses'."
